ALVA — Complete Post-Match Celebration, Match Results, and Dialog Overhaul

Objective

Implement a comprehensive redesign of the end-of-match experience for Quick Battle and Watch Mode in the Alva game.

The goal is to make matches transition naturally into a continuously running post-match celebration instead of stopping gameplay and immediately displaying a blocking results dialog.

Replace the existing end-of-match results flow with:

1. A new non-pausing post-match celebration state.
2. New match-ending announcer messages.
3. Autonomous CPU victory celebration behaviors.
4. A persistent, bottom-centered match outcome toast.
5. A detailed, expandable Match Results dialog.
6. Complete match statistics for both teams.
7. Improved post-match navigation.
8. Consistent close and settings controls on game-pausing dialogs.
9. Roman numeral team naming.
10. Correct post-match Void behavior without respawning.

Implement these changes in the existing codebase, following Alva’s established architecture, visual design, localization, input system, and gameplay conventions.

This is a real implementation task, not a UI mockup.

